---
import Chapter from '../Chapter.astro';
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
import FigPlanes from '../figures/FigPlanes.astro';
import FigHandshake from '../figures/FigHandshake.astro';

const props = [
  {
    t: 'Fail closed',
    d: 'No answer, no path, missing evidence or a validated path that differs from the selected one: the connection is denied, with its reason.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Possession stays with TLS',
    d: 'The engine decides whether the issuer is admissible. Only the TLS stack decides whether the peer holds the private key.',
  },
  {
    t: 'No network in the handshake',
    d: 'Graph, policy and status evidence are compiled beforehand and resident in memory. Governance can be down and admission goes on.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Selection, not authority',
    d: 'A standard library validates the selected path, and only that path. An error of the engine becomes a denial, never an undue acceptance.',
  },
];
---

<Chapter id="admission" num="07" kicker="Admission at the server" title="The decision lives where the connection is accepted.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The work does not end when the model computes a path. It ends when that path decides whether
      a connection gets in. PolarisChain sits in the <strong>server side of an mTLS handshake</strong>:
      the enforcement point is the TLS endpoint's own client-certificate check, and the decision
      point runs in the same process, with no proxy and no network in between.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each domain splits the work in two planes that can fail separately: an asynchronous
      governance plane that compiles the graph, and an execution plane on the critical path of the
      handshake.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure num={6} caption="Two planes in the receiving domain. Adapted from Annex I of the thesis.">
    <FigPlanes />
  </Figure>

  <div class="props grid-4">
    {
      props.map((p) => (
        <div class="rule-top">
          <h3>{p.t}</h3>
          <p class="small">{p.d}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <details class="more">
    <summary>The handshake, step by step</summary>
    <Figure num={7} caption="mTLS admission governed by PolarisChain, with the PEP at the server endpoint and a local PDP. Adapted from Annex II of the thesis.">
      <FigHandshake />
    </Figure>
  </details>
</Chapter>

<style>
  .props {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .props h3 {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }
  .props .small {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .more {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .more summary {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--link);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .more summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .more summary::before {
    content: '+';
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .more[open] summary::before {
    content: '−';
  }
  .more .figure {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
</style>
